  "scope": "Compare the existing LS-proxy estimator with independent morphology-supported stellar references on held-out objects in one common-coverage control field. Matched LS and COSMOS counterparts share the same holdout key. Source selection probabilities are not system detection probabilities. No physical background transfer, mutual cluster crowding, independent-sky validation, HSC passband identity, or 0706 confirmation is inferred. Morphology/SED agreement is an independent reference, not perfect truth. IR detection selection, incomplete/ambiguous matches, epoch/proper-motion effects, native HSC bandpasses and quoted uncorrected errors remain explicit limitations. Holdout separates matched counterpart IDs in one sky; close blends and common image/background correlations remain. Conditions are source-sampled, not uniform-sky completeness depths. The selected column is PS1 DR2 joint selection. Intermediate counts share the full reference denominator; do not multiply joint losses again."
